OAKLAND TECH DIGEST
Friday, September 18, 2026

Hi neighbors,

A full week ahead, and the Startup Week schedule is live. Here is what is on.

THIS WEEK
- The Oakland Startup Week schedule is up: 38 sessions over five days, October 12 to 16, including a hardware track at Fifth Street Foundry and a founders-only breakfast each morning at Ninth Street Commons. https://oaklandtechdigest.org/startup-week
- The Foundry's membership waitlist is closed again after the September 8 reopening filled in nine days. Next opening is planned for January.

COMING UP
- Tue Sep 22, 6:00pm | Uptown Hardware Meetup at Fifth Street Foundry. This month's theme: putting sensors on old machines. Two show-and-tells and open shop time. Free. https://oaklandtechdigest.org/e/hw-sep22
- Thu Sep 24, 5:30pm | Climate Tech Happy Hour, Jack London Square. Hosted by three East Bay climate-hardware companies; first drink covered. https://oaklandtechdigest.org/e/climate-sep24
- Sat Sep 26, 10:00am | Kids coding morning, Dimond Library. Ages 6 to 10, laptops provided, parents stay. Registration required. https://oaklandtechdigest.org/e/kids-sep26
- Tue Sep 29, 8:00am | Founders Coffee, Temescal. Same place, same big table.

COMMUNITY
- Ninth Street Commons is running open-house hours next week ahead of its October 1 opening; drop by weekday afternoons.
- The Saturday volunteer day moved about two tons of equipment into the Foundry's new bay. Thank you to the 30-odd people who showed up.

JOBS BOARD
- Embedded software engineer, Berkeley (medical devices)
- Shop manager, Fifth Street Foundry
- Customer success lead, Oakland (logistics software)
Post a job: https://oaklandtechdigest.org/jobs

See you around the lake,
Desmond

